# Plan — Consolidate SLA / DPA / Subprocessor structure (Drive)

_Live state as of 2026-06-02. Shared drive: **Normain** (`0ADHH7JidkICFUk9PVA`). No file is deleted: moves within the shared drive preserve file ID, link, and version history; superseded copies go to an `old/` / `99. Old/` folder._

## Agreed design decisions

| # | Decision |
|---|---|
| 1 | Customer-facing policies (Privacy Policy, Cookie Policy, Terms of Use) + default published agreements live as **single masters in `01 - SaaS default agreements`**, not in InfoSec. (Move keeps the file link valid; the InfoSec update-runbook path gets repointed; optional shortcut left in InfoSec for ISMS discoverability.) |
| 2 | **Marketplace DPA and SaaS DPA are separate lineages** — Marketplace = privacy-first, SaaS = experimentation-first — kept in separate folders even while currently identical. |
| 3 | **Versioning unit = the DPA.** SLA is never versioned standalone — each DPA version carries a **copy of the SLA as an attachment**. |
| 4 | Templates split into **two motion folders**: `01 - Microsoft Marketplace Templates` + `02 - Customer Cloud Hosting Templates`. DPA templates inside are **versioned by date — one dated folder per {DPA + Subprocessor list}**. |

Combined versioning unit (decisions 3+4): **one dated folder = { DPA + SLA copy + Subprocessor-list snapshot }**.

